{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793070000000-engineer-8f3b.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-15 10:30:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-15 17:30:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: 8f-3 fix round 1: Architect P3 items 1-4 (uncommitted, additive and tiny)\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-15 17:30 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: same author continues; Fable already signed off the base diff; orchestrator restores two parity pins\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8f3 holds your uncommitted 8f-3 diff: keep every hunk byte-identical except as below. Read ./collab/1792055212830-architect-8f3-review.report.md section P3 items 1-4 (item 5 style: fix too if trivial). DO: (1) fix the loaded-code-floor docstring at src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc ~:978 as suggested; (2) add the envelope refusal pin: one assertion in semantic_stream_observer_test (or the test that exercises test_utils run-encoder-session) that an envelope whose :yin/root is out of range is refused with {:rule :batch-envelope}, exercising test_utils.cljc:170-176; (3) in effects_test/blocked-put add the blocked-WRITER EDN round trip pin (entry survives pr-str/read-string and the revived entry still retries its value), as the Architect describes, mirroring the old blocked-entries-are-pure-data second block (git show HEAD:test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc); (4) restore a docstring for code-address in src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc (\"the dao.jing segment address of a canonical vector. UCF mints no second addressing scheme.\"); (5) collapse the triple blank lines. Nothing else. No docs, no src/yang, no commit/stage. Foreground lanes: kondo on the changed files; clojure -M:test -e :slow -n for the changed test namespaces and yin.vm.ucf-adjacent ones that load ucf (yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test, yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize-test). R